  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{y}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{(\\mathrm{x}+1)^{2}(\\mathrm{x}+2)}$. Then $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}^{2} \\mathrm{y}}{\\mathrm{dx}^{2}}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2\\left[\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{4}}-\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$3\\left[\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{(x+1)^{2}}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{3}}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{6}{(x+1)^{3}}-\\frac{4}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{7}{(x+1)^{3}}-\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\nBy partial fraction technique\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\ny=\\frac{x^{2}}{(x+1)^{2}(x+2)}=\\frac{4}{(x+2)}-\\frac{3}{(x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow y^{\\prime \\prime}=\\frac{6}{(x+1)^{4}}-\\frac{6}{(x+1)^{3}}+\\frac{8}{(x+2)^{3}}\r\n\\end{array}$"
  }
}